    {
      "bbox": [
        420,
        1914,
        1350,
        2092
      ],
      "category": "List-item",
      "text": "(a) Within six months of the effective date of this Order, the Inspector General of each agency shall be responsible for the preparation and prosecution of all formal administrative proceedings, including removal and other disciplinary proceedings for misconduct or incompetence, initiated by such Inspector General or any other person authorized by the agency head to initiate such proceedings on behalf of the agency. The Inspector General or an attorney-designee (including attorneys of the Department of Investigation) shall prosecute such matters. Any agency head may for good cause apply to the Commissioner for the modification or waiver of any provision of this paragraph.",
